WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.792
Welcome to Module 11, Advanced S Q L in Postgres.

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:09.637
Before we begin, connect this module to what you already know.

00:00:09.637 --> 00:00:17.782
You have learned how to filter and aggregate data, join tables, use subqueries, work with strings and dates,

00:00:17.782 --> 00:00:19.532
clean messy values, and reshape data.

00:00:19.532 --> 00:00:26.102
In Module 10, you also learned to protect the grain of a result.

00:00:26.102 --> 00:00:28.500
That idea remains important here.

00:00:28.992 --> 00:00:32.359
Now we will build more advanced analytical queries.

00:00:32.359 --> 00:00:38.209
We will use common table expressions to break complicated logic into clear stages.

00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:42.214
We will use recursive queries to move through hierarchies.

00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:48.959
And we will use window functions to rank rows, compare one event with an earlier or later event,

00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:54.914
calculate running totals, and create moving averages without losing the detail rows.

00:00:54.914 --> 00:00:58.399
The goal is not to memorize difficult syntax.

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:05.352
The goal is to understand what each stage is doing, what one row represents, and why the result is correct.
